'''''Xerotricha gasulli''''' is a [[species]] of air-breathing [[land snail]], [[Terrestrial animal|terrestrial]] [[pulmonate]] [[gastropod]] [[mollusk]]s in the family [[Geomitridae]], the hairy snails and their allies.<ref name="WoRMS">MolluscaBase eds. (2022). MolluscaBase. Xerotricha gasulli (Ortiz de Zárate López, 1950). Accessed through: World Register of Marine Species at: https://www.marinespecies.org/aphia.php?p=taxdetails&id=1002563 on 2022-07-31</ref>

==Distribution==
[[File:Xerotricha-gasulli-map-eur-nm-moll.jpg|thumb|left|Distribution]]
This species is [[Endemism|endemic]] to [[Spain]].

